meta {
  name: Join Own Session
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/requests
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.error.code: eq CANNOT_JOIN_OWN_SESSION
}

docs {
  Implemented (half of D4). Runs with `auth: inherit` -- the collection's default token,
  i.e. the **host** -- against the session they themselves created.
  `CreateRequestUseCase` checks `userId === session.host.id` right after loading the
  session and throws `CannotJoinOwnSessionError` before touching the request repository.

  **Known gap -- the other half of D4 is still missing:** the same use case never checks
  `session.status !== OPEN`, so joining a `FULL` or `CANCELLED` session isn't rejected
  (`SessionNotOpenError`). No Bruno test for that yet since there's no easy way to drive a
  session to `FULL`/`CANCELLED` in this collection's current flow.
}
